{
	"_comment": "How many backend calls one prediction request takes, replayed through _shared/ai/engine/request_plan/batching.lua by the macOS and Linux runners and through LLM_RequestPlanBatching by the Windows runner. A batch profile asks once for every variant when more than one is requested; every other case asks once per variant. This is the rule of ai/engine/settings/profile_selector.lua (a batch prompt is a batch only above one prediction). per_call is the number of variants one call returns, which also scales that call's token budget. expect_error is a substring of the message the plan must raise. sequential_mode is llm.generation.sequential_mode (PPT-03): concurrent says whether the calls of one request may overlap, false when it is on, for a single call and for a batch.",
	"vectors": [
		{
			"id": "a-batch-profile-asks-once-for-every-variant",
			"batch_profile": true,
			"requested": 3,
			"sequential_mode": false,
			"expect": {
				"mode": "batch",
				"calls": 1,
				"per_call": 3,
				"concurrent": false
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "sequential-mode-leaves-a-batch-one-call",
